// Row-level security: one dynamic role, "Desk".
//
// Modeling → Manage roles → New → name it Desk, then add a DAX filter on each table:
//
// ---- table: dim_route -------------------------------------------------------------
// A person sees a route when its origin is one of their airports in user_access.
// Filtering dim_route filters fact_fare_quote and quarantine through the relationships.

dim_route[origin]
    IN CALCULATETABLE (
        VALUES ( user_access[origin] ),
        user_access[email] = USERPRINCIPALNAME ()
    )

// ---- table: user_access -------------------------------------------------------------
// People see only their own access rows, so nobody can read who else sees what.

user_access[email] = USERPRINCIPALNAME ()

// Why this is safe by default: an email that is not in user_access matches no rows,
// so a typo or a new joiner sees an empty report, not everything. "*" (all airports)
// is expanded into one row per airport when the warehouse is built, so the rule never
// needs a special case.
//
// Emails are compared as Power BI returns them from USERPRINCIPALNAME(). The export
// stores them lower-case; if your tenant returns mixed case, wrap both sides in LOWER().
